# WHAT THIS FILE IS: the answers upstream llama.cpp gave for this checkpoint, on the
# same device this port runs on. Unlike a fixture this port captured of itself, it can
# show that this port is wrong rather than only that it changed. The values are
# log-probabilities over the full vocabulary, because that is the only quantity
# llama-server exposes; a replay converts its own logits the same way before comparing.
# The prompt is the raw prompt file, no chat template, sent as text and tokenized by
# the reference with its own add_special. This checkpoint declares NO opening token -
# its tokenizer_config.json says `bos_token: null` - so add_special adds nothing, the
# header above carries no `leading_token`, and a replay prepends nothing. The per-case
# tokens_digest is over the prompt's own ids and no others.
# WHEN IT FAILS: this port disagrees with an independent implementation of the same
# checkpoint. Name the case and the diverging rank, dump that row, and walk the ops.
# Never widen the budget.
